{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GJ9toP8xVV6Uih6J9qD4tr","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Phase 1: Planning Mode\n     2→\n     3→You are an architect. Generate or update IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md.\n     4→\n     5→## Absolute Rules\n     6→- DO NOT implement anything. Planning only.\n     7→- DO NOT modify any source code files.\n     8→- DO NOT create source files.\n     9→- You MAY create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md and update AGENTS.md\n    10→\n    11→## Process\n    12→\n    13→### 1. Gather Context\n    14→Read the following with parallel subagents:\n    15→- All files in `specs/*` — the requirements\n    16→- `CLARITY_LOG.md` — resolved ambiguities and decisions from Socratic phase\n    17→- Existing source code in `src/*` (if any) — what's already built\n    18→- `src/lib/*` — shared utilities and components\n    19→- **External API docs** — if specs reference external libraries/APIs, run `chub search \"<library>\"` then `chub get <id>` to fetch up-to-date documentation. Save fetched docs to `.context/` so the build phase can reference them. This prevents planning around outdated or hallucinated APIs.\n    20→\n    21→### 2. Gap Analysis\n    22→Use an Opus subagent with ultrathink to compare specs + clarity decisions against existing code:\n    23→- What is specified but not yet implemented?\n    24→- What is implemented but not matching specs?\n    25→- What integration points are needed?\n    26→- What shared utilities should be extracted?\n    27→\n    28→### 3. Generate/Update IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n    29→\n    30→```markdown\n    31→# Implementation Plan\n    32→Generated: <ISO timestamp>\n    33→Total_Items: <N>\n    34→Completed: <M>\n    35→Test_Items: <T> (target: ≥70% of implementation items)\n    36→\n    37→## Dependency Graph\n    38→<!-- The harness uses this section to identify items that can be built in parallel -->\n    39→```\n    40→Independent_Groups:\n    41→  - group_1: [Item 1, Item 3, Item 5]   # no dependencies between these\n    42→  - group_2: [Item 2, Item 4]           # depends on group_1\n    43→  - group_3: [Item 6]                   # depends on group_2\n    44→Build_Order: group_1 → group_2 → group_3\n    45→```\n    46→\n    47→## Item <N>: <concise title>\n    48→- status: TODO | IN_PROGRESS | DONE | BLOCKED\n    49→- priority: P0 | P1 | P2\n    50→- complexity: S | M | L | XL\n    51→- depends_on: [Item <X>, Item <Y>]\n    52→- spec: specs/<filename>.md\n    53→- clarity_ref: CLARITY_LOG.md#Round-<N> (if relevant)\n    54→- description: <what to build, one paragraph>\n    55→- acceptance: <how to verify it works — concrete, testable criteria>\n    56→- tests: <what tests to write for this item>\n    57→```\n    58→\n    59→### 3.5 Complexity Estimation Criteria\n    60→Assign complexity based on these criteria (the harness uses this for model routing):\n    61→\n    62→| Complexity | Criteria | Model |\n    63→|------------|----------|-------|\n    64→| **S** (Small) | Single file, <50 LOC, well-defined pattern | Sonnet |\n    65→| **M** (Medium) | 2-3 files, <200 LOC, standard patterns | Sonnet |\n    66→| **L** (Large) | 4+ files, 200-500 LOC, cross-module logic | Opus |\n    67→| **XL** (Extra Large) | System-wide changes, >500 LOC, novel patterns | Opus |\n    68→\n    69→### 4. Planning Rules\n    70→- P0 items MUST have no unresolved `depends_on` to TODO items\n    71→- Every implementation item MUST have a companion test item (or tests: field)\n    72→- Test items count toward the 70% test code target\n    73→- Items should be small enough that ONE agent session can complete ONE item\n    74→- \"One sentence test\": if you need \"and\" to describe what an item does, split it\n    75→- Infrastructure/setup items go first (P0)\n    76→- Core business logic second (P0-P1)\n    77→- UI/integration last (P1-P2)\n    78→- **Maximize parallelism**: group items with no mutual dependencies together. The harness can build independent items simultaneously.\n    79→- **Prefer S/M items**: splitting L/XL items into S/M items enables more parallelism and cheaper model routing\n    80→\n    81→### 5. Persist\n    82→```bash\n    83→git add IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md AGENTS.md\n    84→git commit -m \"plan: <N> items, <M> P0, <T> test items, <G> parallel groups\"\n    85→```\n    86→\n    87→## Exit Condition\n    88→IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md exists with at least one item and all items have valid status/priority/complexity/acceptance fields. Dependency Graph section is present. Write at the last line:\n    89→```\n    90→PHASE_1_COMPLETE\n    91→```\n    92→\n    93→## Important\n    94→- Don't assume anything is missing — search the codebase first\n    95→- Prefer fewer, well-scoped items over many vague ones\n    96→- Each item's acceptance criteria should be verifiable by running a test\n    97→- The build phase will pick items in priority order, so get priorities right\n    98→- The Dependency Graph section is critical — the harness uses it for parallel execution\n    99→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XcJCBKsi68fQQZ4rhmBqCD","session_id":"80a1a421-27b4-4bc6-b3a0-5a170dfc59c6","uuid":"8240130c-f6cf-4a1d-b33e-1a8a8cd9be08"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SDBAzRCEVijNtXLyo1VtEh","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→# Phase 2: Building Mode\n     2→\n     3→You are a builder. Implement exactly ONE item per session.\n     4→\n     5→## Session Start Routine (do this every time)\n     6→1. `pwd` — confirm working directory\n     7→2. Read `progress.txt` — what happened recently\n     8→3. Read `LEARNINGS.md` — runtime discoveries from previous iterations (if exists)\n     9→4. Read `IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md` — find highest priority TODO\n    10→5. `git log --oneline -10` — recent changes\n    11→6. **Fetch docs** — if the TODO item uses external APIs/libraries, run `chub search \"<library>\"` then `chub get <id>` to fetch up-to-date documentation. Save to `.context/` for reference. This prevents hallucinating outdated APIs.\n    12→7. Run the project's test suite — verify current state is green\n    13→8. If tests fail, fix them FIRST before starting new work\n    14→\n    15→## Rules\n    16→- Pick the HIGHEST PRIORITY item with status `TODO` from IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n    17→- Update its status to `IN_PROGRESS` immediately\n    18→- Before modifying anything, SEARCH the codebase — don't assume not implemented\n    19→- Use parallel subagents for search and read operations\n    20→- Use only 1 subagent for build and test operations (prevents file conflicts)\n    21→- Implement functionality COMPLETELY. No placeholders. No stubs. No TODOs in code.\n    22→- Write tests BEFORE or alongside implementation\n    23→- Target: 70% of your code should be test code\n    24→\n    25→## Implementation Flow\n    26→```\n    27→1. Search codebase for related code (parallel subagents)\n    28→2. Write/update tests for the acceptance criteria\n    29→3. Implement the feature to make tests pass\n    30→4. Run full test suite\n    31→5. Run typecheck (if applicable)\n    32→6. Run lint (if applicable)\n    33→7. All green? → commit. Any red? → fix in THIS session.\n    34→```\n    35→\n    36→## After Implementation\n    37→1. Update item status to `DONE` in IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md\n    38→2. If you discovered new items needed, add them with appropriate priority and complexity\n    39→3. Append to `progress.txt`:\n    40→   ```\n    41→   === Session <timestamp> ===\n    42→   Completed: Item <N> - <title>\n    43→   Changes: <brief summary>\n    44→   Why: <reasoning behind key decisions>\n    45→   Discovered: <any new issues or items added to plan>\n    46→   Difficulty: <was complexity estimate accurate? S/M/L/XL actual vs planned>\n    47→   ```\n    48→4. Update AGENTS.md ONLY if you learned something operational (build commands, patterns)\n    49→5. Keep AGENTS.md under 60 lines — trim if needed\n    50→6. **Update LEARNINGS.md** — append any discoveries that future iterations should know:\n    51→   ```\n    52→   ### Learning: <title>\n    53→   - Context: <what you were doing>\n    54→   - Discovery: <what you learned>\n    55→   - Rule: <concrete rule for future iterations>\n    56→   ```\n    57→   Examples of valuable learnings:\n    58→   - Import path conventions discovered (e.g., `@/` prefix required)\n    59→   - API quirks found (e.g., \"Stripe webhook needs raw body, not parsed JSON\")\n    60→   - Build system behaviors (e.g., \"must run `prisma generate` after schema change\")\n    61→   - Patterns established (e.g., \"all error types extend BaseError\")\n    62→7. **Annotate external API learnings** — if you discovered API behavior not in docs:\n    63→   ```bash\n    64→   chub annotate <library-id> \"<discovery>\"\n    65→   ```\n    66→   This persists across sessions so future iterations benefit automatically.\n    67→8. Commit:\n    68→   ```bash\n    69→   git add -A\n    70→   git commit -m \"<type>: <description of what and why>\"\n    71→   ```\n    72→\n    73→## Backpressure Checklist (must ALL pass before commit)\n    74→- [ ] Typecheck passes\n    75→- [ ] Lint passes\n    76→- [ ] ALL tests pass (not just new ones)\n    77→- [ ] No `it.skip`, `@pytest.mark.skip`, or disabled tests\n    78→- [ ] No placeholder/stub implementations\n    79→- [ ] No console.log/print debugging left behind\n    80→\n    81→## Critical Patterns\n    82→- \"don't assume not implemented\" — ALWAYS search first\n    83→- \"capture the why\" — commit messages explain reasoning\n    84→- \"single source of truth\" — no adapters, no migration layers\n    85→- \"implement completely\" — stubs waste iterations redoing work\n    86→- \"read LEARNINGS.md\" — don't repeat mistakes from previous iterations\n    87→\n    88→## Failure Reporting\n    89→If you CANNOT complete the item in this session, clearly report WHY:\n    90→```\n    91→BUILD_ITEM_FAILURE:\n    92→  item: <N>\n    93→  reason: COMPILE_ERROR | TEST_FAILURE | DEPENDENCY_MISSING | COMPLEXITY_UNDERESTIMATE | API_ISSUE\n    94→  detail: <specific error or blocker>\n    95→  suggestion: RETRY | SPLIT | ESCALATE | SKIP\n    96→  split_into: [<sub-item descriptions if suggestion=SPLIT>]\n    97→```\n    98→This helps the harness make intelligent recovery decisions.\n    99→\n   100→## Exit\n   101→After completing exactly ONE item and committing, stop. The loop will restart you with fresh context.\n   102→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01XcJCBKsi68fQQZ4rhmBqCD","session_id":"80a1a421-27b4-4bc6-b3a0-5a170dfc59c6","uuid":"c5b5771a-7502-461c-933f-2014fdbc0522"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XcJCBKsi68fQQZ4rhmBqCD","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the comprehensive context. Let me create a summary of the findings:\n\n## Comprehensive Project Context Summary\n\n### 1. **Specification (specs/employee-crud-api.md)**\n\n**Project Overview:**\n- Legacy Spring 4 MVC REST API for employee management (AS-IS migration tool input)\n- Java 1.8, Spring Framework 4.3.4, MyBatis 3.2.2, PostgreSQL (with H2 for tests)\n- Stateless HTTP Basic Auth, no Spring Boot\n\n**Entity: Employee**\n| Field | Type | Constraints |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| id | Long | PK, auto-increment |\n| name | String | NOT NULL, 1–100 chars |\n| email | String | NOT NULL, unique, valid email |\n| department | String | NOT NULL, 1–50 chars |\n| salary | BigDecimal | NOT NULL, >= 0 |\n| hireDate | Date | NOT NULL |\n| createdAt | Timestamp | auto-set on insert |\n| updatedAt | Timestamp | auto-set on insert/update |\n\n**REST Endpoints:**\n- `GET /api/employees` — list (paginated, USER role)\n- `GET /api/employees/{id}` — get by ID (USER role)\n- `POST /api/employees` — create (ADMIN role, returns 201 + Location header)\n- `PUT /api/employees/{id}` — full replacement (ADMIN role, returns 200)\n- `DELETE /api/employees/{id}` — delete (ADMIN role, returns 204)\n- `GET /api/employees/search` — search by name/department (USER role, paginated)\n\n**Authentication:**\n- HTTP Basic Auth with in-memory users:\n  - `admin/admin123` → ADMIN\n  - `user/user123` → USER\n\n**Architecture:**\n```\ncom.example.legacy/\n├── config/          (AppConfig, WebConfig, SecurityConfig, DatabaseConfig, WebInitializer)\n├── model/           (Employee, PageResult)\n├── mapper/          (EmployeeMapper interface)\n├── service/         (EmployeeService interface + impl)\n├── controller/      (EmployeeController, GlobalExceptionHandler)\n├── dto/             (EmployeeRequest, ErrorResponse)\n└── validation/      (EmployeeValidator)\n```\n\n**MyBatis XML Mapper Methods:**\n- findAll, findById, insert (with useGeneratedKeys), update, delete, countAll, searchByNameOrDepartment, findByEmail\n\n### 2. **CLARITY_LOG.md (Resolved Ambiguities - Phase 0: Socratic)**\n\n**20 ambiguities resolved with Ambiguity Score = 0.05:**\n\nKey resolutions:\n- **Search endpoint** (R1.1): Query params `name` and `department` (both optional, OR logic, case-insensitive LIKE)\n- **Validation errors** (R1.3): Extend ErrorResponse with `fieldErrors` list containing { field, message }\n- **PUT semantics** (R1.4): Full replacement (all fields required), 404 if not exists\n- **PageResult structure** (R1.5): { content: [...], totalPages, totalElements, currentPage }\n- **POST response** (R1.6): 201 Created with full Employee body + Location header\n- **PUT response** (R1.7): 200 OK with full updated Employee body\n- **DELETE response** (R1.8): 204 No Content, 404 if not exists\n- **Date serialization** (R1.9): hireDate \"yyyy-MM-dd\", timestamps \"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss\" (ISO 8601, no timezone)\n- **Email validation** (R1.13): @Email from javax.validation via Hibernate Validator\n- **H2 compatibility** (R1.11): H2 MODE=PostgreSQL, schema.sql uses PostgreSQL syntax\n- **Test profile** (R1.12): @ActiveProfiles(\"test\"), separate application-test.properties for H2\n- **Search with no params** (R1.18): 400 Bad Request — at least one param required\n- **Duplicate email on update** (R1.19): Exclude self from uniqueness check\n- **Error timestamp format** (R1.20): ISO 8601 string format\n\n### 3. **.harness-config**\n\n```\nPROJECT_TYPE=\"java-maven\"\nBUILD_CMD=\"mvn compile\"\nTEST_CMD=\"mvn test\"\nLINT_CMD=\"mvn checkstyle:check 2>/dev/null || true\"\nTYPECHECK_CMD=\"mvn compile\"\nTEST_CODE_RATIO_TARGET=0.70\nAMBIGUITY_THRESHOLD=0.10\n```\n\n### 4. **pom.xml — Dependencies**\n\n**Core:**\n- Spring Framework 4.3.4.RELEASE\n- Spring Security 4.2.4.RELEASE\n- MyBatis 3.2.2 + mybatis-spring 1.3.2\n- Jackson 2.9.11.1 (JSON)\n\n**Database:**\n- PostgreSQL 42.2.27\n- Commons DBCP2 2.9.0 (connection pooling)\n- H2 1.4.200 (test scope)\n\n**Validation:**\n- javax.validation-api 1.1.0\n- hibernate-validator 5.4.3.Final\n- javax.el 3.0.0\n\n**Logging:**\n- SLF4J 1.7.36\n- Logback 1.2.12\n\n**Testing:**\n- JUnit 4.13.2\n- Mockito 3.12.4\n- spring-test 4.3.4\n- spring-security-test 4.2.4\n- hamcrest 1.3\n- jsonpath 2.7.0\n\n### 5. **AGENTS.md — Operational Guide**\n\n- Build: `mvn compile`\n- Test: `mvn test`\n- Lint: `mvn checkstyle:check 2>/dev/null || true`\n- Patterns: single source of truth, test-first, atomic commits\n- Anti-patterns: no duplicate utilities, don't modify test assertions, no debug logging\n\n### 6. **Current Status**\n\n- **Phase**: Planning Mode (PROMPT_plan.md is active)\n- **Previous Phase**: Socratic (CLARITY_LOG.md completed with ambiguity=0.05)\n- **Source Code**: Completely empty (src/main/ and src/test/ are bare directories)\n- **progress.txt**: Only contains harness initialization timestamp\n- **IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md**: Does not yet exist (needs to be created)\n\n### 7. **Key Technical Constraints**\n\n- **Java 1.8**: No var, no records, no text blocks, no switch expressions; prefer anonymous classes for legacy feel\n- **Spring 4.3.4**: NOT Spring Boot, all configuration explicit Java/XML\n- **MyBatis 3.2.2**: SQL in XML mappers only, no annotations\n- **javax.validation**: NOT jakarta.validation\n- **JUnit 4**: NOT JUnit 5\n- **Test DB**: H2 in-memory with PostgreSQL mode, H2 loads schema.sql but NOT data.sql for test isolation\n\n---\n\n## Summary for Planning\n\nThis is a **greenfield implementation** of a Spring 4 legacy REST API with the following characteristics:\n\n1. **Complete emptiness**: All source code must be written from scratch\n2. **Well-defined requirements**: Spec is comprehensive with 20 resolved ambiguities\n3. **Stack specificity**: Java 1.8 + Spring 4 + MyBatis 3.2 (vintage tech stack)\n4. **High test target**: 70% test code ratio\n5. **Architecture clarity**: Clear package structure defined in spec\n\nThe next phase is **Planning (Phase 1)**: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md with 20+ items covering:\n- Configuration classes (AppConfig, WebConfig, SecurityConfig, DatabaseConfig, WebInitializer)\n- Model & DTO classes\n- MyBatis mapper and XML files\n- Service layer (interface + implementation)\n- Controller and exception handling\n- Validation logic\n- Comprehensive test suite (70%+ test code)\n\n**File Paths for Reference:**\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/specs/employee-crud-api.md` — Requirements\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/CLARITY_LOG.md` — Resolved ambiguities\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/pom.xml` — Dependencies\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/.harness-config` — Build configuration\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/AGENTS.md` — Operational guide\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/progress.txt` — Session history"},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: a49b8b77631967394 (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 33246\ntool_uses: 20\nduration_ms: 38131</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"80a1a421-27b4-4bc6-b3a0-5a170dfc59c6","uuid":"0394913e-2318-4207-8462-f43100ad9330","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to gather comprehensive context for planning an implementation. Please read and summarize ALL of the following:\n\n1. All files in `specs/` directory - these are the requirements\n2. `CLARITY_LOG.md` - resolved ambiguities\n3. All existing source code in `src/` directory (recursively)\n4. `.harness-config` - build configuration\n5. `AGENTS.md` - operational guide\n6. `progress.txt` - recent session context\n7. `pom.xml` - project dependencies and build config\n\nFor source code, I need to understand:\n- What's already implemented\n- What patterns/utilities exist\n- What the project structure looks like\n\nBe thorough - read every file. Start with glob patterns to find all files, then read them all.","agentId":"a49b8b77631967394","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have all the comprehensive context. Let me create a summary of the findings:\n\n## Comprehensive Project Context Summary\n\n### 1. **Specification (specs/employee-crud-api.md)**\n\n**Project Overview:**\n- Legacy Spring 4 MVC REST API for employee management (AS-IS migration tool input)\n- Java 1.8, Spring Framework 4.3.4, MyBatis 3.2.2, PostgreSQL (with H2 for tests)\n- Stateless HTTP Basic Auth, no Spring Boot\n\n**Entity: Employee**\n| Field | Type | Constraints |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| id | Long | PK, auto-increment |\n| name | String | NOT NULL, 1–100 chars |\n| email | String | NOT NULL, unique, valid email |\n| department | String | NOT NULL, 1–50 chars |\n| salary | BigDecimal | NOT NULL, >= 0 |\n| hireDate | Date | NOT NULL |\n| createdAt | Timestamp | auto-set on insert |\n| updatedAt | Timestamp | auto-set on insert/update |\n\n**REST Endpoints:**\n- `GET /api/employees` — list (paginated, USER role)\n- `GET /api/employees/{id}` — get by ID (USER role)\n- `POST /api/employees` — create (ADMIN role, returns 201 + Location header)\n- `PUT /api/employees/{id}` — full replacement (ADMIN role, returns 200)\n- `DELETE /api/employees/{id}` — delete (ADMIN role, returns 204)\n- `GET /api/employees/search` — search by name/department (USER role, paginated)\n\n**Authentication:**\n- HTTP Basic Auth with in-memory users:\n  - `admin/admin123` → ADMIN\n  - `user/user123` → USER\n\n**Architecture:**\n```\ncom.example.legacy/\n├── config/          (AppConfig, WebConfig, SecurityConfig, DatabaseConfig, WebInitializer)\n├── model/           (Employee, PageResult)\n├── mapper/          (EmployeeMapper interface)\n├── service/         (EmployeeService interface + impl)\n├── controller/      (EmployeeController, GlobalExceptionHandler)\n├── dto/             (EmployeeRequest, ErrorResponse)\n└── validation/      (EmployeeValidator)\n```\n\n**MyBatis XML Mapper Methods:**\n- findAll, findById, insert (with useGeneratedKeys), update, delete, countAll, searchByNameOrDepartment, findByEmail\n\n### 2. **CLARITY_LOG.md (Resolved Ambiguities - Phase 0: Socratic)**\n\n**20 ambiguities resolved with Ambiguity Score = 0.05:**\n\nKey resolutions:\n- **Search endpoint** (R1.1): Query params `name` and `department` (both optional, OR logic, case-insensitive LIKE)\n- **Validation errors** (R1.3): Extend ErrorResponse with `fieldErrors` list containing { field, message }\n- **PUT semantics** (R1.4): Full replacement (all fields required), 404 if not exists\n- **PageResult structure** (R1.5): { content: [...], totalPages, totalElements, currentPage }\n- **POST response** (R1.6): 201 Created with full Employee body + Location header\n- **PUT response** (R1.7): 200 OK with full updated Employee body\n- **DELETE response** (R1.8): 204 No Content, 404 if not exists\n- **Date serialization** (R1.9): hireDate \"yyyy-MM-dd\", timestamps \"yyyy-MM-dd'T'HH:mm:ss\" (ISO 8601, no timezone)\n- **Email validation** (R1.13): @Email from javax.validation via Hibernate Validator\n- **H2 compatibility** (R1.11): H2 MODE=PostgreSQL, schema.sql uses PostgreSQL syntax\n- **Test profile** (R1.12): @ActiveProfiles(\"test\"), separate application-test.properties for H2\n- **Search with no params** (R1.18): 400 Bad Request — at least one param required\n- **Duplicate email on update** (R1.19): Exclude self from uniqueness check\n- **Error timestamp format** (R1.20): ISO 8601 string format\n\n### 3. **.harness-config**\n\n```\nPROJECT_TYPE=\"java-maven\"\nBUILD_CMD=\"mvn compile\"\nTEST_CMD=\"mvn test\"\nLINT_CMD=\"mvn checkstyle:check 2>/dev/null || true\"\nTYPECHECK_CMD=\"mvn compile\"\nTEST_CODE_RATIO_TARGET=0.70\nAMBIGUITY_THRESHOLD=0.10\n```\n\n### 4. **pom.xml — Dependencies**\n\n**Core:**\n- Spring Framework 4.3.4.RELEASE\n- Spring Security 4.2.4.RELEASE\n- MyBatis 3.2.2 + mybatis-spring 1.3.2\n- Jackson 2.9.11.1 (JSON)\n\n**Database:**\n- PostgreSQL 42.2.27\n- Commons DBCP2 2.9.0 (connection pooling)\n- H2 1.4.200 (test scope)\n\n**Validation:**\n- javax.validation-api 1.1.0\n- hibernate-validator 5.4.3.Final\n- javax.el 3.0.0\n\n**Logging:**\n- SLF4J 1.7.36\n- Logback 1.2.12\n\n**Testing:**\n- JUnit 4.13.2\n- Mockito 3.12.4\n- spring-test 4.3.4\n- spring-security-test 4.2.4\n- hamcrest 1.3\n- jsonpath 2.7.0\n\n### 5. **AGENTS.md — Operational Guide**\n\n- Build: `mvn compile`\n- Test: `mvn test`\n- Lint: `mvn checkstyle:check 2>/dev/null || true`\n- Patterns: single source of truth, test-first, atomic commits\n- Anti-patterns: no duplicate utilities, don't modify test assertions, no debug logging\n\n### 6. **Current Status**\n\n- **Phase**: Planning Mode (PROMPT_plan.md is active)\n- **Previous Phase**: Socratic (CLARITY_LOG.md completed with ambiguity=0.05)\n- **Source Code**: Completely empty (src/main/ and src/test/ are bare directories)\n- **progress.txt**: Only contains harness initialization timestamp\n- **IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md**: Does not yet exist (needs to be created)\n\n### 7. **Key Technical Constraints**\n\n- **Java 1.8**: No var, no records, no text blocks, no switch expressions; prefer anonymous classes for legacy feel\n- **Spring 4.3.4**: NOT Spring Boot, all configuration explicit Java/XML\n- **MyBatis 3.2.2**: SQL in XML mappers only, no annotations\n- **javax.validation**: NOT jakarta.validation\n- **JUnit 4**: NOT JUnit 5\n- **Test DB**: H2 in-memory with PostgreSQL mode, H2 loads schema.sql but NOT data.sql for test isolation\n\n---\n\n## Summary for Planning\n\nThis is a **greenfield implementation** of a Spring 4 legacy REST API with the following characteristics:\n\n1. **Complete emptiness**: All source code must be written from scratch\n2. **Well-defined requirements**: Spec is comprehensive with 20 resolved ambiguities\n3. **Stack specificity**: Java 1.8 + Spring 4 + MyBatis 3.2 (vintage tech stack)\n4. **High test target**: 70% test code ratio\n5. **Architecture clarity**: Clear package structure defined in spec\n\nThe next phase is **Planning (Phase 1)**: Create IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md with 20+ items covering:\n- Configuration classes (AppConfig, WebConfig, SecurityConfig, DatabaseConfig, WebInitializer)\n- Model & DTO classes\n- MyBatis mapper and XML files\n- Service layer (interface + implementation)\n- Controller and exception handling\n- Validation logic\n- Comprehensive test suite (70%+ test code)\n\n**File Paths for Reference:**\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/specs/employee-crud-api.md` — Requirements\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/CLARITY_LOG.md` — Resolved ambiguities\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/pom.xml` — Dependencies\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/.harness-config` — Build configuration\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/AGENTS.md` — Operational guide\n- `/Users/pinxbot/Desktop/ralph_loop/examples/asis-legacy/progress.txt` — Session history"}],"totalDurationMs":38131,"totalTokens":33246,"totalToolUseCount":20,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3237,"cache_read_input_tokens":27830,"output_tokens":2173,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":3237},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01G3QHwovv5JEfcXU4JnK3NZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have comprehensive context. Let me create the IMPLEMENTATION_PLAN.md. The project is a greenfield Spring 4 MVC REST API for employee management. I need to:\n\n1. Plan all items needed to implement the full spec\n2. Group them by dependencies for parallel execution\n3. Ensure 70%+ test items\n4. Keep items small (S/M complexity preferred)\n5. Include acceptance criteria for each item\n\nLet me design the implementation plan:\n\n**Infrastructure/Config (Group 1 - P0, no dependencies):**\n1. Database schema (schema.sql) + H2 test config - S\n2. AppConfig + DatabaseConfig (datasource, MyBatis) - M\n\n\n3. WebConfig (Spring MVC, Jackson date format) - S\n4. SecurityConfig (HTTP Basic, in-memory users) - M\n5. WebInitializer (servlet setup) - S\n\n**Model/DTO (Group 2 - P0, depends on schema):**\n6. Employee model - S\n7. PageResult model - S\n8. EmployeeRequest DTO - S\n9. ErrorResponse DTO (with fieldErrors) - S\n\n**MyBatis Mapper (Group 3 - P0, depends on models + config):**\n10. EmployeeMapper interface - S\n11. EmployeeMapper.xml - M\n12. EmployeeMapper integration tests with H2 - M\n\n**Validation (Group 3 - can parallel with mapper):**\n13. EmployeeValidator - S\n\n**Service Layer (Group 4 - depends on mapper + validation):**\n14. EmployeeService interface and implementation - M\n15. EmployeeService unit tests with Mockito - M\n\n**Controller + Exception Handler (Group 5 - depends on service):**\n16. GlobalExceptionHandler - S\n17. EmployeeController - L\n18. EmployeeController integration tests - L\n\nNow I'm reconsidering the granularity here. The user wants items small enough that a single agent session can complete one item, and I need to think about test coverage too since the spec targets 70% test code. Let me break this down more carefully to ensure proper parallelization and account for the testing requirements.\n\n**Group 1 - Foundation (No dependencies, all P0):**\n- Item 1: Database schema with test schema - S\n- Item 2: DatabaseConfig with datasource, transaction manager, and MyBatis session factory - S\n- Item 3: AppConfig with component scanning and property sources - S\n- Item 4: WebConfig with MVC setup, Jackson configuration, and content negotiation - S\n- Item 5: SecurityConfig with HTTP Basic authentication, in-memory users, and CSRF disabled - M\n- Item 6: WebInitializer with DispatcherServlet and DelegatingFilterProxy - S\n\n**Group 2 - Models & DTOs (depends on Group 1 for compile context, but functionally independent):**\n- Item 7: Employee model - S\n- Item 8: EmployeeDTO - S\n- Item 9: EmployeeRequest DTO with validation annotations - S\n- Item 10: ErrorResponse DTO with field errors - S\n- Item 11: EmployeeValidator - S\n\nActually, models and DTOs don't really depend on the config classes at all—they're truly independent. Let me map out the actual dependency chain: models and DTOs have no dependencies, config classes are mostly standalone, MyBatis mapper interfaces need the Employee model, the XML mapper needs the interface, the validator needs Employee and EmployeeRequest, the service layer needs the mapper and validator, the controller needs the service and DTOs, and finally the exception handler sits at the top.\n\nSo I'll organize this into two clear groups: first, all the independent pieces like the Employee and PageResult models, the DTOs, the schema, and the web initializer. Then the second group covers everything that depends on those foundations—the config classes, MyBatis components, and the validator.\n\nAfter that, I need the service layer and exception handling, which depend on the mapper and config being in place. The service tests and controller come next, and finally the integration tests for the controller once everything else is ready.\n\nI'm realizing some of these items are too granular though. The instruction about using \"and\" to decide whether to split makes sense, but I should also keep the tasks reasonably sized so they're not trivial.\n\nLet me reconsider the grouping. The config classes are tightly coupled and could work as a single item. The models and DTOs are all small pieces—under 50 lines of code each—so grouping related ones makes sense without losing clarity on what needs testing.\n\nI'll keep the items focused but consolidate where it makes sense: the models can go together since they're straightforward, the DTOs with their validation annotations can be separate since they have different test concerns, and the error response is simple enough to include with something else or stand alone depending on dependencies.\n\nFor the second group, the configuration classes form a natural unit since they're interdependent, while the mapper and validator are distinct enough to warrant their own items. The web initializer is small but critical for wiring everything together.\n\nThe third group focuses on integration testing where everything comes together—the mapper tests need the full stack, and the employee controller tests will depend on all the configuration being in place.\n\nActually, I'm reconsidering the grouping structure. The core constraint is that Spring 4.3.4 requires manual configuration rather than Boot's auto-configuration, and MyBatis 3.2.2 uses XML mappers instead of annotations. Java 1.8 is the target, which means I need to be careful about compatibility.\n\nFor the test infrastructure, I'll need H2 configured for the test environment and PostgreSQL for production. The package structure is clear: config, model, mapper, service, controller, dto, and validation packages. I'll also need test resources including the H2 configuration properties and a schema definition that's compatible with H2, plus a base test class to handle the setup.\n\nNow I'm organizing the implementation into logical groups based on dependencies. First, I'll tackle the pure data classes and schema—the Employee and PageResult models, the request and error response DTOs, and the database schema itself. These have no Spring dependencies and can be built independently.\n\nNext comes the Spring configuration layer along with the mapper and validator, which all depend on those models being in place. This includes the database and application configs for datasource and transaction management, the web config for serialization, security configuration for HTTP Basic auth, the web initializer, the MyBatis mapper interface and XML definition, and the employee validator.\n\nThen I can run the test infrastructure and mapper integration tests in parallel with the service layer, since both depend on Group 2 being complete. The test infrastructure sets up the test config and base classes, while the service layer implements the EmployeeService and the global exception handler. I realize the service layer actually needs both the mapper and validator from Group 2, so once that group finishes, both the test infrastructure and service layer can proceed simultaneously.\n\nFor Group 4, I'm looking at the service unit tests and the controller. The controller handles all the CRUD endpoints plus search functionality, which feels like it should stay as one item since it's a single class with consistent patterns. I'm also thinking about the test coverage target of 70% test items, so I need to make sure I'm accounting for enough testing tasks throughout the breakdown. I need to hit the 70% test coverage target based on implementation items, not code lines. With 14 implementation items planned, I need around 10 test items to meet that threshold. Let me structure the plan pragmatically with the core models and DTOs as independent pieces, then build the configuration and service layers on top of them.\n\nContinuing with the mapper, validator, and test infrastructure in the second group, followed by service and exception handling in the third group. The fourth and fifth groups focus on unit and integration tests for the service and controller layers, ensuring comprehensive coverage across all the critical paths.\n\nNow I'm realizing the test coverage is only about half the total items, so I should expand the controller tests more granularly—breaking them down by endpoint type and cross-cutting concerns like authentication and validation rather than lumping them together.\n\nLet me work out a more realistic split: roughly 14 implementation items and 10 test items, which gives me better coverage. I'll organize this into dependency groups starting with the models and DTOs, then the configuration and infrastructure, and finally the business logic and tests. I'm realizing the test-to-implementation ratio is still falling short at around 53%. The issue is that I've got too many small configuration and model items scattered throughout. Let me reorganize by bundling closely related small tasks together so they form more substantial work items.\n\nI'm grouping the models and DTOs into one cohesive item, combining the database setup with its test configuration, consolidating all the Spring configs, and treating the mapper, validator, and exception handler as individual pieces. For the controller, I'm splitting the test coverage into separate integration test suites focused on different concerns—CRUD operations, search and pagination, and authentication with error handling. This gives me 11 implementation items and 9 test items, which hits 82% test coverage. That feels right for a well-tested application. Now I'm laying out the second group of tasks covering configuration and infrastructure setup—the DatabaseConfig, WebConfig, and SecurityConfig that wire everything together, plus the MyBatis mapper and validator, along with test infrastructure to support integration testing. The third group then focuses on testing the mapper, building out the service layer, and adding global exception handling.\n\nLooking at the remaining groups, I've got c